# Test: a refused enum value at the editor `set` proposes the accepted values
# QUESTION: does an operator at the SSH editor, typing a value outside an
#   enumeration, read the shared refusal with the fix written in the form they
#   typed, the whole of it in the viewport while the prompt stays? A unit test
#   proves the text; only the editor run proves the operator sees it there.
# VALIDATES: spec-config-enum-refusal AC-6 -- root form at the root, relative
#   form inside `edit bgp peer peer1`, `top set` form behind `top` (AC-48);
#   nothing stored.
# PREVENTS: `invalid value "requre" for route-refresh (expected enum)`.

tmpfs=test.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
  router-id 1.2.3.4;
  session {
    asn {
      local 65000;
    }
  }
  peer peer1 {
    connection {
      remote {
        ip 1.1.1.1
      }
    }
    session {
      asn {
        remote 65001
      }
    }
  }
}
EOF_CONF

option=file:path=test.conf
option=timeout:value=10s

# At the root: the root form.
input=type:text=set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh requre
input=enter
expect=error:contains=bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh: "requre" is not an accepted value (did you mean require?)
expect=viewport:contains=route-refresh accepts only these values:
expect=viewport:contains=fix: set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh require
expect=viewport:not-contains=expected enum

# Inside the peer: the relative form typed.
input=type:text=edit bgp peer peer1
input=enter
input=type:text=set session capability route-refresh requre
input=enter
expect=viewport:contains=fix: set session capability route-refresh require
expect=context:path=bgp/peer/peer1

# Behind `top` inside the peer: the fix keeps `top`.
input=type:text=top set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh requre
input=enter
expect=viewport:contains=fix: top set bgp peer peer1 session capability route-refresh require
expect=context:path=bgp/peer/peer1

# Nothing was stored.
input=type:text=top show
input=enter
expect=viewport:not-contains=requre
